    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnaequābĭlĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		inaequabilis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>inequality</i>, <i>unlikeness</i>,
				<i>variety</i> (postclass. and very rare), <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, 3, 108</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elementorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 81</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Gramm. t. t., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνωμαλία,</span>
			<i>want of uniformity</i>, <i>anomaly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermonis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, 1, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
